\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4.1}{\ignorespaces DTS-GSSF architecture. The input tensor $\mathbf {X} \in \mathbb {R}^{B \times T \times N \times F}$ flows through the Gated Recurrent Encoder (temporal encoding), GraphPropagation (spatial diffusion), TemporalAttention (long-range dependencies), and Prediction Heads (per-station and aggregate forecasts).}}{17}{figure.caption.10}%
\addvspace {10pt}
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Open data benchmark overview. Monthly boardings and active stop counts for the LACMTA evaluation dataset.}}{29}{figure.caption.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Performance comparison on the LACMTA open dataset. DTS-GSSF achieves the highest $R^2$ and the lowest MAE compared to baselines.}}{29}{figure.caption.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Average ridership by city sub-region in the Los Angeles open dataset. The central and mid-city districts show the highest demand, while the peripheral South Bay region has lower average boardings.}}{30}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Ablation study results. Bars show test $R^2$ for each architectural variant; the dashed line indicates the full model (v3). Removing GraphPropagation (v1) causes the largest performance drop, while the TemporalAttention module (v2$\to $v3) provides the second-largest improvement.}}{31}{figure.caption.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Per-horizon test-set accuracy: $R^2$ and MAE across 15, 30, 60, and 120 minute prediction horizons.}}{32}{figure.caption.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Training and validation loss curves across 3 independent seeds. Shaded regions indicate $\pm 1$ standard deviation.}}{33}{figure.caption.21}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces Calibration analysis. Left: Expected Calibration Error (ECE) across distributional output heads (lower is better). Right: Quantile coverage at 50\% and 90\% credible intervals. Dashed lines indicate nominal coverage levels.}}{35}{figure.caption.23}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.8}{\ignorespaces Normalized feature importance from Integrated Gradients attribution (20 reference points, zero-feature baseline, $n = 20$ test windows).}}{36}{figure.caption.24}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.9}{\ignorespaces Per-district test-set performance. Left: $R^2$ by district. Right: MAE by district. The central Esil district achieves the highest accuracy, while the peripheral Baikonur district shows the largest errors.}}{37}{figure.caption.26}%
